WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.608 --> 00:00:05.390
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Becca, how's it going?

2
00:00:06.846 --> 00:00:09.658
Becca Lund: Hi Tom. Pretty good. How are you?

3
00:00:10.861 --> 00:00:19.868
Tom Lindqvist: I'm doing well, thanks. It's been a busy couple of weeks on my end, but nothing too crazy. How's everything in Sioux Falls?

4
00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:26.234
Becca Lund: We got our first snow last night. Just a dusting, but it's officially here.

5
00:00:27.094 --> 00:00:28.551
Tom Lindqvist: Already? That feels early.

6
00:00:29.975 --> 00:00:38.382
Becca Lund: It is a little early, but honestly I'd rather have snow than the wind we had all last week. My commute was brutal.

7
00:00:38.852 --> 00:00:46.530
Tom Lindqvist: Fair enough. So I wanted to check in on the training session we've got on the calendar for November 10.

8
00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.951
Becca Lund: Yes, that's still on. Six new hires starting that Monday, so the timing works well.

9
00:00:52.706 --> 00:00:57.194
Tom Lindqvist: Good. Do you know who all needs logins set up before then?

10
00:00:58.006 --> 00:01:06.410
Becca Lund: Let me pull up my list. I've got the six names here. I can send them over this afternoon.

11
00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:15.733
Tom Lindqvist: That would be great. Once I have the list, I'll get the logins created so everyone's ready to go on day one.

12
00:01:16.048 --> 00:01:25.203
Becca Lund: Perfect. Three of them are coming from our call center in Fargo, so they'll need the same access as the rest of that team.

13
00:01:25.945 --> 00:01:29.722
Tom Lindqvist: Okay, I'll note that. Same permissions as the Fargo group.

14
00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:34.964
Becca Lund: Right. The other three are local here in Sioux Falls.

15
00:01:35.779 --> 00:01:42.275
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. And are you planning to run the session, or do you want me to lead it?

16
00:01:42.976 --> 00:01:51.979
Becca Lund: I was hoping you could take the first part, the overview stuff, and then I'll walk them through our day-to-day workflows.

17
00:01:52.800 --> 00:02:00.157
Tom Lindqvist: That works. I'll put together a refresher version of the overview, nothing too long. Maybe thirty minutes?

18
00:02:01.052 --> 00:02:06.080
Becca Lund: Thirty minutes is good. Their attention spans are short on day two.

19
00:02:06.308 --> 00:02:18.006
Tom Lindqvist: Ha, understood. I'll keep it tight. Do you want me to send a calendar invite to the group, or should I send it to you and you forward it?

20
00:02:18.528 --> 00:02:27.504
Becca Lund: Send it to me and I'll forward it. Some of them don't have their work email set up until their first day.

21
00:02:28.665 --> 00:02:32.704
Tom Lindqvist: No problem. I'll get that out by end of week.

22
00:02:34.089 --> 00:02:43.455
Becca Lund: Thanks. Now, holiday call volume. I'm expecting the usual spike around Thanksgiving and then again the week between Christmas and New Year's.

23
00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:53.749
Tom Lindqvist: That lines up with what I usually see. Do you want to adjust anything on your end for that stretch?

24
00:02:54.995 --> 00:03:01.548
Becca Lund: We're adding a couple of extra shifts, mostly on the outage side. Nothing we can't handle.

25
00:03:02.396 --> 00:03:07.872
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. If anything changes, just let me know and we can look at it together.

26
00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:13.471
Becca Lund: Will do. Honestly, last year was fine, so I'm not expecting surprises.

27
00:03:14.013 --> 00:03:17.833
Tom Lindqvist: Good to hear. How's the rest of the team doing?

28
00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:26.916
Becca Lund: Everyone's good. We had a team lunch last Friday, which was nice. First one we've done in a while.

29
00:03:28.045 --> 00:03:31.404
Tom Lindqvist: That sounds fun. Anything good on the menu?

30
00:03:32.594 --> 00:03:37.050
Becca Lund: Just pizza. But it was the good pizza place, so no complaints.

31
00:03:37.255 --> 00:03:41.368
Tom Lindqvist: Can't go wrong with that. Oh, how's the new puppy?

32
00:03:41.885 --> 00:03:49.608
Becca Lund: Oh, he's a terror. Chewed through a phone charger already. But he's cute, so he gets away with it.

33
00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:51.949
Tom Lindqvist: What kind is he?

34
00:03:53.236 --> 00:04:00.843
Becca Lund: A lab mix. My daughter picked him out. She's been begging for a dog for two years, so here we are.

35
00:04:01.922 --> 00:04:07.655
Tom Lindqvist: That's how it always starts. Well, congrats. Or condolences, one of the two.

36
00:04:08.071 --> 00:04:10.118
Becca Lund: Both, honestly. But he's settling in.

37
00:04:11.575 --> 00:04:15.961
Tom Lindqvist: Glad to hear it. Anything else on your radar before the holidays?

38
00:04:17.413 --> 00:04:21.468
Becca Lund: Not really. Things are going fine, just the usual busy season stuff.

39
00:04:22.472 --> 00:04:29.421
Tom Lindqvist: Good. Then I'll send the invite by Friday and get the logins ready once I have your list.

40
00:04:29.911 --> 00:04:32.251
Becca Lund: Perfect. I'll get you those names today.

41
00:04:32.491 --> 00:04:34.556
Tom Lindqvist: Sounds good. Talk soon, Becca.

42
00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.270
Becca Lund: Thanks, Tom. Have a good one.
